# continuation-licence.rq (loop O, 2026-08-03) — THE CONTINUATION LICENCE (residue R33).
#
# Open-world derivation (CLAUDE.md §8): "the pair (N-1, N) the recognition AXIOM licensed may
# actually be STITCHED" is GROWN from evidence both pages carry — the NON-TABLE text blocks the
# renderer drew around the table. Every input is a presence fact emitted by
# document.licence_evidence (one node per non-table block: its exact text, which page it sits on,
# and whether it sits at the CONSTRAINED position), so this query carries NO numeric literal, no
# threshold and no tolerance. A pair whose evidence does not meet the law stays UNLICENSED, and an
# unlicensed pair is two independent documents: recognition alone never stitches.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. continuation-of.rq recognizes that page N redraws page N-1's header block on the
# same author grid. That is necessary but NOT sufficient for "one table" — two INDEPENDENT
# documents built from one TEMPLATE share exactly that evidence (measured, loop M task 2 review;
# residue R33, taxonomy case 2 vs case 3). The discriminator R33 names is the BODY side, and it is
# not text reading: a paginated table is CUT by the page edge, so what surrounds it either repeats
# on both pages (page furniture: running head, footer) or is new content — and new content around
# the table on the continuation page means a new document, not a continuation.
#
# READING vs COMPARING (the same distinction continuation-of.rq draws, and for the same reason —
# see its header's READING-vs-COMPARING block, which this query inherits verbatim in spirit). The
# law compares two renderings of the SAME string for literal identity. It draws no meaning from any
# string — no keyword, no "looks like a banner" judgment, no page-number recognition. Asking "did
# the renderer draw this block again on the other page?" is evidence comparison; asking "what does
# this block say?" would be reading, and would belong to NEURAL (§8).
#
# THE LAW (asymmetric — the asymmetry is load-bearing; stated verbatim from the loop-O plan):
#   a recognized pair is licensed iff
#     (a) every non-table block on page N outside the repeated header block has a text-identical
#         counterpart block on page N-1 (page-invariance), AND
#     (b) every block on page N-1 below the table's last body row has a text-identical counterpart
#         on page N.
#   Head-side blocks above/before page N-1's table are UNCONSTRAINED.
# WHY THE HEAD SIDE IS FREE: a document's opening furniture (its title, its print timestamp) is
# drawn ONCE, on the first page, and legitimately so — the stem's title band and print timestamp
# are p0-only. A symmetric invariance law would read that opening furniture as "page N-1 carries
# something page N does not" and refuse the GENUINE stitch. The cut runs between page N-1's tail
# and page N's head, so those are the two sides the law constrains; what page N-1 carried before
# its table says nothing about whether its table was cut.
# Both counterpart tests are unrestricted on the answering side: a block at the constrained
# position may be answered by ANY block on the other page, wherever it sits. Position matters only
# for whether a block must be ANSWERED, never for what may answer it.
#
# VACUITY IS LICENCE, deliberately: a pair whose pages carry no non-table block at all (two bare
# tables, nothing around them) meets both clauses trivially and is licensed. That is the
# fluent-reader invariant cutting the other way — two indistinguishable bare tables on consecutive
# pages ARE read as one continued table by a human reader, so stitching them is the correct
# reading, not a false positive. The law refuses on MARKS; absent marks it does not invent one.
#
# WHAT THIS LAW REFUSES THAT IT SHOULD NOT — MEASURED ON THE STEM, 2026-08-03 (honest, §7)
# The 3-page GrainCorp stem (corpus/ag-trade/graincorp-stem-2026-07-31.pdf) is a GENUINE case-2
# pagination, and this law as stated REFUSES both of its pairs. Its non-table blocks, measured:
#   * a running head, p0/p1/p2, identical text on all three ("GRAINCORP SHIPPING STEM /
#     GrainCorp Operations Ltd ABN 52003875401") — invariant, licenses;
#   * a p0-only 'SHIPPING STEM' band above the table — head side, unconstrained, correctly free;
#   * a footer band at top=573.87 on all three pages whose LINE ends with the PAGE NUMBER:
#     "GrainCorp advise that the load dates shown are indicative only and are subject to change 1"
#     / "... 2" / "... 3". It sits BELOW the table on every page, so it is constrained by clause
#     (b) on the prior side AND by clause (a) on the continuation side, and its text is NOT
#     identical across the pair. Both clauses refuse.
# The page number defeats the law at EVERY block granularity (band, line, or word run: the numeral
# is its own word at x0=419.04 with no counterpart on the other page), and it is structurally
# INDISTINGUISHABLE, without reading, from the marked case-3 banner the law is built to refuse —
# both are "same laid-out position, different text". Recorded here rather than worked around: the
# refinement is the loop controller's call, and no tuned constant or string-meaning test may be
# used to make this one document pass (CLAUDE.md §8; MEMORY "no overfitting").
#
# ROLE OF THE PAGE INDEX: none. The pair is chosen by the caller; the law reads only the two
# pages' block inventories it is given, and the prior/continuation SIDE those blocks were emitted
# on. Nothing here counts pages, blocks or anything else.
PREFIX tab: <https://w3id.org/iladub/tab#>
SELECT ?pair WHERE {
  ?pair a tab:ContinuationPairUnderTest .
  # CLAUSE (a) — PAGE N CARRIES NOTHING NEW. Every block of the continuation page that lies
  # outside the repeated header block must be one the prior page also drew. The ?t join IS the
  # identity test (literal identity — no normalisation, no fuzzy match), exactly as
  # continuation-of.rq's clause (b) joins on ?t.
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?pair tab:hasPageBlock ?cur .
    ?cur a tab:ContinuationPageTextBlock .
    ?cur a tab:OutsideRepeatedHeaderBlock .
    ?cur tab:blockText ?t .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?pair tab:hasPageBlock ?prior .
      ?prior a tab:PriorPageTextBlock .
      ?prior tab:blockText ?t .
    }
  }
  # CLAUSE (b) — PAGE N-1's TAIL SIDE IS FURNITURE, NOT CONTENT. Whatever the prior page drew
  # BELOW its table's last body row must reappear on page N; if it does not, that page's table
  # was not cut by the page edge — something else followed it, and the pages are two documents.
  # A prior block that carries no tab:BelowTableBodyBlock type simply never matches this pattern:
  # that is where the head side's freedom lives, as a pattern that cannot reach it rather than as
  # an exception carved out of it.
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?pair tab:hasPageBlock ?prior2 .
    ?prior2 a tab:PriorPageTextBlock .
    ?prior2 a tab:BelowTableBodyBlock .
    ?prior2 tab:blockText ?t2 .
    FILTER NOT EXISTS {
      ?pair tab:hasPageBlock ?cur2 .
      ?cur2 a tab:ContinuationPageTextBlock .
      ?cur2 tab:blockText ?t2 .
    }
  }
}
